{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>L'ozni.</b> Rashi explained: I say that this is the family of Etzbon, and I do not know, etc., thus far. And it does not seem right to posit something that has no rationale and is not from the words of the Sages of blessed memory. And furthermore it is difficult, for in Midrash Rabbi Tanchuma they said, and this is their language: When you enumerate the family of Gad, there is no Etzbon there, for he was diminished because of the harlotry at the counsel of Bilaam, thus far. Therefore it would appear that Ozni is another family that came forth from Gad, for through general expansion there were in every tribe other branches besides those from whom the family was built, and they were named after their brothers; and sometimes that branch would grow and the family would be called by its name. However, I found in the Pesikta, and this is their language: Ozni — this is Etzbon, for it says in the portion of Vayigash (Genesis 46:16), from the expression of אצית והאזין (paying heed and listening), thus far. According to this, it is the same name itself, and Scripture is not particular about a change of name when the first name is implied in its meaning. And Rashi of blessed memory — the holy spirit rested upon him and he aligned with the words of the Sages of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:48.100841925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}